<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păgăsa</span></b> , ae,
		and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păgăsae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παγασαί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a maritime town of Thessaly</i>, <i>afterwards called</i> Demetrias, <i>where the Argo was built</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbem Pagasam amplexus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 20, 17</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 8, 451</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 8,
				15, § 29</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pă-găsaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pagasa</i>, <i>Pagasœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					2, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 401</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puppis,</span>”
				<i>the Argo</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					7, 1</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called carina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 13, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jason,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 8, 349</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux Pagasaea,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Alcestis</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 3, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păgăsēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Pagasœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puppis,</span>”
				<i>the Argo</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 422</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păgăsĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Pagasœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 8, 15, § 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 12, 23,
				§ 72</span></i>.</div>
